@* The administrators' handbook (FR-117). Until 2026-10 it was a separate HTML file
   (docs/handover/admin-manual.html), printed to PDF and checked against the system by hand — a
   line-by-line audit was needed to find where the two had drifted apart. As a page it changes in
   the same commit as the feature it describes, so when you change how something works, change its
   section here too.

   Written for the people who run the bookings, not for developers: plain Swedish, the exact labels
   they see on screen in bold, steps as numbered lists, and the reason behind a rule where knowing
   it prevents a mistake. Keep it that way.

   Administratör only. Samordnare get Del B on its own page (/handbok/samordnare); the part is one
   shared component (HandbookCoordinatorPart), so it cannot drift between the two.

   Deliberately Static SSR, like /listor: it is reading matter, so it needs no circuit.

   Every in-page link is written "/handbok#…", never a bare "#…": App.razor sets <base href="/">,
   which resolves a bare fragment against "/", so "#avboka" took the reader to the dashboard
   (caught by the E2E test that clicks a contents link, 2026-10-13).

   Building blocks are the legal pages' document structure (.legal-block, .prose, .subhead,
   .data-table), .card for numbered steps and .alert for the boxes — warn for "this goes wrong if
   you don't", info for explanations. Tables carry data-label on every cell but the first, which
   .data-table--stack uses to turn each row into a stacked block on a phone.

   Layout (.handbook--with-toc): one fluid column — text, tables and boxes alike — that fills the
   admin frame like every other admin page, and from 68.75em the contents list in a sticky column
   beside it.
   Narrower, the list is a box between the introduction and Del A, which is also where it sits in
   the markup. Check a layout change by rendering it at several widths: the first version fixed
   everything at 65ch and was the same 584px at every window width. *@
@page "/handbok"
@layout AdminLayout
@attribute [Authorize(Roles = AdminRoles.Administrator)]

<PageTitle>Handbok — Åkerögården Admin</PageTitle>

<AdminHeader Title="Handbok" />

<div class="handbook handbook--with-toc">

    <section class="legal-block handbook__intro">
        <div class="prose">
            <p><b>Vad det här är.</b> En handbok för er som arbetar i Åkerögårdens bokningssystem — inte en teknisk beskrivning. Den täcker det ni gör i vardagen: ta emot en förfrågan, godkänna den, hämta listorna till köket, lägga in en bokning som kommit per telefon, hålla byggnader, mat och priser aktuella — och vad varje status och varje mejl från systemet betyder.</p>
            <p><b>Två adresser.</b> Gästerna besöker <b>akerogarden.se</b>. Ni arbetar här, på <b>admin.akerogarden.se</b>. Det är samma system men två skilda webbplatser — gästerna kommer aldrig åt er sida.</p>
            <p><b>Två sorters konton.</b> <b>Administratör</b> ser och gör allt. <b>Samordnare</b> (kök och praktiskt ansvariga) ser bara deltagarlistor, matlistor och sin del av den här handboken (<a href="/handbok#del-b">Del B</a>, under <b>Handbok</b> i deras meny) — inga kontaktuppgifter, inga andra sidor.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

